From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: adapted-for-msm8998
Date: Mon, 20 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cgroup: restore prefixed symlink under CGRP_ROOT_NOPREFIX

Droidspaces/LXC compatibility for non-GKI 4.4 trees.

When a hierarchy is mounted with "noprefix", cgroup control files are
created without the subsystem prefix. Create an additional
"<subsys>.<file>" kernfs link so userspace that expects the prefixed
name still works.

Adapted for SGCMarkus/android_kernel_lge_msm8998 (kernel/cgroup.c):
- use name vs legacy_name like cgroup_file_name()
- warn on link creation failure

---
 kernel/cgroup.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/kernel/cgroup.c b/kernel/cgroup.c
--- a/kernel/cgroup.c
+++ b/kernel/cgroup.c
@@ -3490,6 +3490,18 @@ static int cgroup_add_file(struct cgroup_subsys_state *css, struct cgroup *cgrp,
 		spin_lock_irq(&cgroup_file_kn_lock);
 		cfile->kn = kn;
 		spin_unlock_irq(&cgroup_file_kn_lock);
 	}
+
+	/*
+	 * Under CGRP_ROOT_NOPREFIX the real file has no "subsys." prefix.
+	 * Create a compatibility symlink: subsys.file -> file
+	 * (mainly useful for cpuset hierarchies mounted with noprefix).
+	 */
+	if (cft->ss && (cgrp->root->flags & CGRP_ROOT_NOPREFIX) &&
+	    !(cft->flags & CFTYPE_NO_PREFIX)) {
+		const char *ssn = cgroup_on_dfl(cgrp) ? cft->ss->name
+						     : cft->ss->legacy_name;
+
+		snprintf(name, CGROUP_FILE_NAME_MAX, "%s.%s", ssn, cft->name);
+		if (kernfs_create_link(cgrp->kn, name, kn))
+			pr_warn("cgroup: failed to create prefix link %s\n", name);
+	}
 
 	return 0;
 }
